# Follow-up to 2026-09-29-19.play. That run (druid:guardian, mash, escort,
# 1280x800) had the tracked body die at fightTime~107 and every further
# chained `play` call abort in 0s on the already-documented hero()===null
# driver gap ("Tried and dropped" in direction.md), so the match's real
# outcome was never seen -- only that both carts read a near-static 31%/57%
# right up to the point polling stopped, which does not look like the rout
# 2026-09-27-19's conquest tank-mash pull produced (126-400). This script
# does the workaround that note names but nobody has run yet: mash to first
# blood, then drop chained `play` entirely and poll with bare wait/state so
# a death does not stop the driver from watching the rest of the match.
open
tap battleground
tap map:escort
tap class:druid:guardian
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state

play mash 100
shot mid1
state
bill

wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
wait 20
state
shot late
bill
says
